Exploratory branch, isolated from A0–V1 (no lean_lib, no Comparator suite).
I_T[(1,∅),(0,(2))] = ∫_{T̃} (L − P₁) P₂ computed exactly via Proposition 10.2's
stratification (rough set, inclusion–exclusion, Dirichlet aggregates); the
rational arithmetic is kernel-checked row by row (decide +kernel, standard
axioms), with kernel refutations as negative controls and exact (N = 1, 2)
and Monte Carlo (N = 3, 45) cross-checks. NOTES.md records the cap-sequence
discrepancy in Lemma 9.1's proof, symmetry counts and complexity estimates.

